    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0788" n="754" xml:id="pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 BE/1–854</note>
                <head>No. 329<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to Foreign Minister Bidault</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d329-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-08">January 8, 1954</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I appreciate very much your prompt reply<anchor n="2" xml:id="d329-f2"/> to my
                    suggestion that you, Mr. Eden, and
                    myself meet together prior to the Berlin Conference.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d329-f3"/> In view of the reservations which both you and Mr.
                        Eden have with respect to a meeting
                    with Chancellor Adenauer, I will defer to
                    your wishes.</p>
                <p>With respect to the place of our meeting, I am impressed with the reasons
                    advanced for meeting in Berlin, particularly because of the uncertainties of
                    flying weather. Therefore, I am agreeable to the suggestion that we arrive in
                    Berlin on January 22nd and have the 23rd, and if necessary the 24th, for our
                    talks, if this is convenient to you.</p>
                <p>Since we are not to meet with Chancellor Adenauer before the Berlin Conference, I think it is important
                    that he know we wish to maintain close contact with him on those aspects of the
                    Berlin Conference relating to Germany, and with this in mind, would you see
                    objection to our having a brief meeting in Berlin with Dr. Grewe prior to January 25 in order to make his
                    acquaintance? I plan to have Ambassador Conant with me in Berlin for those meetings concerning Germany
                    and assume you and Mr. Eden will also
                    have your High Commissioners there. In these circumstances, Dr. Grewe would presumably be a channel of
                    communication with Chancellor Adenauer
                    which our representatives will frequently use.</p>
                <p>I am sending a similar message to Mr. Eden.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
